diagnostic_evidence.quote:
We consider Wahba's problem for the case of two vector observations such that

\begin{align}
	f(\qq) = \sum_{\ell= 1}^2 \Abs{\qq[][-1]\qa[\ell]\qq - \qb[\ell]}^2 = 0.

Hence, $(\qa[1] + \qa[2]) \sim (\qb[1] + \qb[2])$, that is there exists a nonzero quaternion $\qq$ such that

\begin{align}
	\qq[][-1](\qa[1] + \qa[2])\qq = \qb[1] + \qb[2].
